// Core Region surface — ALLOCATOR STORY STAGE 1 (contract only).
//
// `Region` is the allocator boundary: allocation is an explicit CAPABILITY,
// never ambient state — no Omega program allocates without holding a Region
// (the name follows Cathedral's resource model; a region frees its memory in
// bulk on its own drop, while element cleanup stays a chapter 16 drops
// concern of the values themselves).
//
// STAGE 1 declares only this contract surface: the trait exists so code and
// designs can NAME the boundary, and so the `alloc`/`dealloc` effects
// (chapter 18 effect names) attach to the machines that will carry them. No
// provider is bound, no runtime exists, and nothing in core requires a
// Region yet — stage 1 containers (core/fixed_vec.omg) are deliberately
// allocator-free. Stage 2 binds Region implementations through the reserved
// `Allocation` boundary-provider category (host malloc vs Cathedral arena
// per target) and introduces `Vec<'r, T>` borrowing a region.
//
// The machines speak raw extents (`size`/`align` in bytes, addresses as
// `usize`): the typed-container story sits ABOVE this boundary; the boundary
// itself is exactly what a kernel arena or host malloc can honor.

boundary trait Region {
    machine allocate(size: usize, align: usize) -> usize
    effects
        alloc;

    machine deallocate(address: usize, size: usize, align: usize)
    effects
        dealloc;
}
